# Proposed narrow correction; no acceptance or new scientific run

Root and a separate source-exposed reviewer identified the compensation-bound wording and the retained-moment ambiguity in the frozen 818699a3 derivation. They also identified aliasing in a saved fixture record. These findings were exposed before this correction; no blind or independent discovery is claimed. Other reviewer checks remain ongoing. This directory is a proposed corrected source for root/reviewer inspection, not a publication or acceptance result.

DERIVATION.md is the complete frozen source with only three affected locations changed; CORRECTION.diff is its exact unified diff. Section 9 now gives compensation peak/action and total peak as upper bounds. Section 10 defines explicitly centered retained-operator moments, proves their bounds using arbitrary bounded test operators, gives the raw binomial identities and marginal/cross-term allowances, and preserves a positive scalar-baseline counterexample with an arbitrarily small SWAP-overrotation fault. It distinguishes scalar variance, linear retained records and conditional/measurement notions. This covers the enlarged-F case where K acts on E and unsymmetrized partial moments can be non-Hermitian.

The section 11 evidence qualification preserves the actual frozen aliasing defect: the final state_before_pivot_phase row holds the post-phase amplitude (48+64i)/125, while the analytic pre-phase amplitude is real16/25. Source inspection shows that the final target comparison actually occurs after the intended phase; its equality check, pair positivity/unitarity identities and routing checks do not use the mislabeled diagnostic record. HISTORICAL_RECORD_EXCERPT.json copies the saved fields and saved predicate; it is not a new calculation. PROPOSED_FIXTURE_REPAIR.diff changes only the diagnostic list capture to state.copy(). It is unexecuted and supplies no new scientific outcome. The original 31 predicates remain dated evidence from2026-10-15 13:32:57 for the unchanged selected routing/synthesis portion, not evidence for this analytic correction.

The original candidate, all its35 sealed files and its freeze remain unchanged. Exact body/code/output/freeze pins and copied premise sources are in SOURCE_MANIFEST.json and sources/. The entire original freeze is checked by metadata only. No new invocation, import or replay of any scientific fixture occurred. No original source, W, Git, PR, audit, prompt, axiom, lock or other chat was mutated. Model/effort were inherited with no override or delegation. Editable prompt files changed: none.

The correction began at2026-10-15 14:03:45 UTC. Metadata receipts record actual source capture and final hash verification. They are author bookkeeping records, not preregistration, scientific validation or institutional independence. The complete correction diff was read without truncation before sealing; later edits only clarified the same counterexample/record scope and historical file references.
